Hmm.  More critique comin'!
Well, I'm really enjoying NetHack 3.0.10.  One thing that really gets to me,
though, is how fast I get hungry.

I _do_ realize there is a reason we get hungry so often.  It does prevent
us from lingering on a level just for experience points.

But 3.0 is silly.  2.3 did the job.  In 2.3 there was a REAL fear of dying
of starvation.  It _was_ fair.  That was motivation enough not to linger
on a level.

I have a hard time picturing a r.p.g. where the adventurers don't eat outside
before entering the dungeon, and then have to eat almost everything they kill
just in order not to die of starvation.

The monsters are more dangerous.  I love that!  It's fun to get killed by
some horendous monster.  It's no fun to be hungry all the time, get weak,
lose strength, die of starvation, even when you're a fairly aggresive
explorer.

The fact is:  In 3.0  we do get hungry disproportionately fast.  And that
is NOT fun.  Meaner levels, mosters, gadgets, gods _are_ fun.  You can
let your imagination get carried away with you.  But to eat everything you
see and still die of starvation is not fun.

flame off. :-)

